{"w":2400,"lines":[{"t":"Test 3","x":0.085436893264348585,"h":0.014641744548286595,"w":0.060194174448649079,"y":0.042056074907950713,"c":1},{"x":0.083495145958350225,"y":0.24127906957552003,"w":0.015533979733784994,"h":0.01308139551465759,"c":1,"t":"F"},{"h":0.01308139551465759,"t":"H","c":1,"y":0.70784883704463342,"w":0.015533979733784994,"x":0.087378641103981275},{"w":0.75353057861328121,"t":"Using wood to construct buildings, however, is not straightforward. Wood expands as it","x":0.12616133306351229,"y":0.088478201361271935,"h":0.021468501818885599,"c":1},{"t":"absorbs moisture from the air and is susceptible to pests, not to mention fire. But treating","w":0.75728154500325529,"h":0.017468123272571967,"c":1,"x":0.13009709149020285,"y":0.10901162779377105},{"t":"wood and combining it with other materials can improve its properties. Cross-laminated","y":0.12642800073675242,"w":0.75157033284505204,"x":0.13004646514900231,"c":1,"h":0.019316042249447829},{"c":1,"h":0.0188953482844747,"x":0.13009708776967102,"w":0.71262135823567707,"y":0.14534883748289906,"t":"timber is engineered wood. An adhesive is used to stick layers of solid-sawn timber"},{"w":0.75947769165039047,"x":0.1299834701510407,"c":1,"t":"together, crosswise, to form building blocks. This material is light but has the strength of","y":0.16286165078736403,"h":0.022085706764292445},{"w":0.7708737691243488,"x":0.13009709949122347,"h":0.017483517536864501,"c":1,"t":"concrete and steel. Construction experts say that wooden buildings can be constructed at a","y":0.18313953514934034},{"c":1,"t":"greater speed than ones of concrete and steel and the process, it seems, is quieter.","w":0.69337081909179688,"x":0.12999585724098087,"y":0.20170970029997481,"h":0.021469370524088482},{"t":"Stora Enso is Europe's biggest supplier of cross-laminated timber, and its vice-president","y":0.2382439045386795,"c":1,"x":0.13003503991785759,"h":0.019835711565344472,"w":0.75352554321289067},{"y":0.25715576934331441,"w":0.73803243001302077,"h":0.020204740149952549,"x":0.13002223304352858,"c":1,"t":"Markus Mannström reports that the company is seeing increasing demand globally for"},{"t":"building in wood, with climate change concerns the key driver. Finland, with its large","y":0.27598842244014521,"x":0.1300459735753311,"w":0.73021316528320324,"h":0.020910715834002502,"c":1},{"h":0.017507064082540769,"t":"forests, where Stora Enso is based, has been leading the way, but the company is seeing","y":0.29651162779409179,"c":1,"w":0.74757283528645835,"x":0.13009707740271173},{"x":0.1300970975197876,"w":0.73980580647786454,"h":0.019003115264797588,"c":1,"t":"a rise in demand for its timber products across the world, including in Asia. Of course,","y":0.31246105943140701},{"c":1,"x":0.13003403980286965,"w":0.76711563110351577,"y":0.33202764241229632,"t":"using timber in a building also locks away the carbon that it absorbed as it grew. But even","h":0.018936541073047541},{"t":"treated wood has its limitations and only when a wider range of construction projects has","h":0.019837104345779122,"y":0.35004128344174623,"w":0.76130116780598966,"c":1,"x":0.13002610725506003},{"h":0.019626502158857306,"x":0.13004974787236714,"c":1,"t":"been proven in practice will it be possible to see wood as a real alternative to concrete in","y":0.36914094911194772,"w":0.75544316609700524},{"w":0.23300971984863281,"h":0.017568644704848424,"c":1,"y":0.38940809957497402,"x":0.13009708174483972,"t":"constructing tall buildings."},{"c":1,"h":0.019014887349256493,"y":0.4242990656265565,"t":"Fly ash and slag from iron ore are possible alternatives to cement in a concrete mix. Fly ash,","w":0.78252426147460941,"x":0.13009709986949122},{"h":0.020266619055441915,"y":0.44332152150341342,"c":1,"x":0.130007651629442,"t":"a byproduct of coal-burning power plants, can be incorporated into concrete mixes to make","w":0.77299392700195302},{"h":0.017553249252176828,"y":0.46355140201834755,"w":0.75339808146158849,"c":1,"x":0.13009707569701656,"t":"up as much as 15 to 30% of the cement, without harming the strength or durability of the"},{"y":0.48102888356229045,"h":0.02039781374352001,"c":1,"x":0.13003822197729695,"w":0.76128835042317711,"t":"resulting mix. Iron-ore slag, a byproduct of the iron-ore smelting process, can be used in a"},{"x":0.13009707896975159,"w":0.77281555175781258,"y":0.49999999987235322,"c":1,"t":"similar way. Their incorporation into concrete mixes has the potential to reduce greenhouse","h":0.017445482866043638},{"x":0.12996873027051001,"w":0.12829934438069659,"c":1,"y":0.52030225935822627,"t":"gas emissions.","h":0.016833902519440058},{"x":0.13191993474816457,"h":0.022744698687877207,"y":0.55381269163369151,"c":1,"t":"But Anna Surgenor, of the UK's Green Building Council, notes that although these waste","w":0.75947143554687502},{"x":0.13195025751763875,"w":0.72829238891601544,"h":0.020096899490118725,"t":"products can save carbon in the concrete mix, their use is not always straightforward.","c":1,"y":0.5740765406407764},{"y":0.59439252363855211,"h":0.017526081120856518,"x":0.13009708530502478,"t":"'It's possible to replace the cement content in concrete with waste products to lower the","c":1,"w":0.74951456705729158},{"c":1,"y":0.61183800648376385,"t":"overall carbon impact. But there are several calculations that need to be considered across","h":0.019003115264797477,"w":0.78058252970377606,"x":0.132038837439374},{"y":0.6299718593873358,"x":0.13003544733181202,"t":"the entire life cycle of the building - these include factoring in where these materials are","w":0.75548243204752585,"h":0.020769645714685536,"c":1},{"y":0.64970930259769288,"w":0.78640777587890631,"t":"being shipped from. If they are transported over long distances, using fossil fuels, the use of","x":0.13203883049009296,"h":0.018895348284474811,"c":1},{"c":1,"w":0.76711629231770839,"t":"alternative materials might not make sense from an overall carbon reduction perspective.?'","y":0.66705740198667696,"x":0.1319822621259012,"h":0.020907162580163341},{"w":0.7378640747070313,"x":0.13009708886575425,"h":0.017592190062145519,"c":1,"y":0.7063953487215624,"t":"While these technologies are all promising ideas, they are either unproven or based on"},{"y":0.72383720956794495,"w":0.75145629882812504,"c":1,"h":0.017595812241979147,"t":"materials that are not abundant. In their overview of innovation in the concrete industry,","x":0.13203884832865573},{"x":0.1319860507140341,"t":"Felix Preston and Johanna Lehne of the UK's Royal Institute of International Affairs","y":0.7426665445345465,"w":0.7224405924479167,"h":0.018625876168224309,"c":1},{"t":"reached the conclusion that, 'Some novel cements have been discussed for more than","c":1,"y":0.75581562796413948,"w":0.72854100545247391,"x":0.13179344875159738,"h":0.026869688895632571},{"w":0.72427185058593757,"h":0.017591284517187167,"x":0.13203883208311709,"y":0.7803738318647796,"c":1,"t":"a decade within the research community, without breaking through. At present, these"},{"h":0.020962667019567727,"c":1,"x":0.13196045637512138,"y":0.79788372556905629,"w":0.77492502848307288,"t":"alternatives are rarely as cost-effective as conventional cement, and they face raw-material"},{"t":"shortages and resistance from customers.'","w":0.3614379628499349,"y":0.81681142827199671,"h":0.019268327041578437,"x":0.13191016336359326,"c":1},{"h":0.01308139551465759,"y":0.95930232543902427,"t":"62","c":1,"x":0.087378640872506949,"w":0.025242718060811353}],"h":3209}